WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.730
Hey, it's B-Pro.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.660
Oh, wow! There are so many of them.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.190
I love them.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.990
Let's take some pictures on the way back.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.490
Thank you for your help.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.990
And thank you for the wonderful song, sir.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.330
Oh, wow! They're so cool.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.160
This kind of thing suits them, too.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.790
<b>Barking Dogs</b>

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.850
I heard it did pretty well in France.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.100
I wonder if we'll get to meet the actors.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.510
I bet it's tough to get in.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:36.760
B-Pro's members react 
exceptionally well to our listeners.

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:36.760
<b>Toranomon Radio</b>

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.400
I hope they'll appear as guests 
on next week's show, too.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.970
Thank you.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.350
<i>Today's guest is B-Project.</i>

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.110
<b>Prince</b>

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.230
It's out.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.410
I'd better buy it before it gets 
damaged by browsing customers.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.120
<b>Top Singles Ranking Jan-Jun</b>

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.120
<b>Kodo Ambitious</b>

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.540
Hey, it's B-Pro.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.810
Did you watch yesterday's <i>Music Train</i>?

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:18.050
<b>Fan Book On Sale!!</b>

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:14.360
Yeah. The new Star Curry commercial was on.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.050
<i>Everywhere I go,
everyone's talking about B-Pro.</i>

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:22.490
<i>It's hard to believe their appearance 
at the FMJ Festival was canceled.</i>

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.340
This is Sumisora.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.370
<i>Good work today.</i>

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:31.320
<i>Tsubasa-san, can you come back 
to the office right away?</i>

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.050
Huh?

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.430
<i>I have some very important news.</i>

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.810
Even the presidents are here?

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.000
I have a feeling this is the 
most important matter since

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.590
the members of B-Pro were announced.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.180
Is it good news or bad news?

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.920
Yashamaru-san, just tell us already.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.800
You boys are hopeless.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.660
You'll be performing at the 
Japan Dome on New Year's Eve!

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.270
Congratulations, guys.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.270
All right!

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:33.990
We did it!

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.680
Yeah, we did it!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.410
Jeez.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:47.040
How long have you had this planned?

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.410
I believed in them.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:53.040
I can't believe we're really 
going to the Japan Dome.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:55.040
This isn't a dream, right?

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:57.500
It's not a dream.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.290
Don't get carried away.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.340
The real battle starts now.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.510
You're right.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.740
Your attitude should be that of someone 
who's just made it to the starting line.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:07.760
Yes, sir.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.420
President, thank you.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.570
Yashamaru-san and Tsubasa, too.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.730
This is thanks to you 
and all the rest of the staff.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:22.090
We'd better give back to all 
our fans who love us, too.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.240
Let's definitely make this a successful show.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.000
Yeah!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.250
Don't cry yet.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.050
Yashamaru-san.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:38.660
Yes, sir. I'll work my hardest 
to make the Dome concert a success.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:43.900
Guys, is there anything 
you want to do at the concert?

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:44.800
I know!

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.170
Since we're performing at a huge venue, 
I want to do something grand!

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:49.260
We agree!

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.620
Maybe we can all parachute in.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:55.730
Hikaru, the Dome has a roof.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.440
How about 20-meter-tall mega costumes?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.150
This isn't the Kohaku.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:03.480
Since it'll be winter, let's make 
snow sculptures of ourselves.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.340
Modern technology is incredible.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.160
Every year, there's a super-cute giant 
sculpture of Mamirin at the snow festival.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.910
We don't have that kind of space.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.490
I know you all have things you want to do,

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.930
but we need to come up with an overall theme.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.840
A theme, huh?

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.820
Since it's New Year's Eve, 
how about a countdown?

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.120
A countdown?

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.480
Countdown bench press.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:27.580
Why?

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.590
Good idea. We need to get in shape.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:30.930
We're not doing that!

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.370
I'll pass your suggestions along.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:35.890
Tsubasa.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:39.570
I'll come up with a tentative plan.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:45.080
Tsubasa-chan, have you come up with a set list?

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.230
Yes, sir.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.490
Here it is.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:56.030
Your song choice isn't bad, 
and your structure is beautiful.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.050
But it's kind of plain.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.130
The song we're debuting at the Dome 
should come at the climax of the show.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.390
Think it over again.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:08.340
Yes, sir.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.350
Do you have a message for your fans 
who are also looking forward

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:12.980
to your Dome performance?

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:13.890
Well...

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.850
We promise we'll exceed their expectations.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:22.770
Yashamaru-san, about the filming 
on the day of the concert...

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:25.690
<i>Make sure you check in with the techs.</i>

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.120
<i>I'm having them set up 
more cameras than usual.</i>

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.540
We're getting pretty used to the new song.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:37.880
And its peculiarities actually 
make it easier to dance.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:41.170
You're right. It's like 
the song pulls our bodies along.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:43.680
No wonder the composer is so successful.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.130
I'm excited to perform it at the Dome.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:47.760
Excuse me.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:49.480
Tsubasa-chan.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:52.890
Good work, everyone. This is for you.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.030
All right!

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.810
Thank you, Sumisora-san.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.430
Those look delicious.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:06:59.810
They're cute.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.810
I see. It's Halloween out there.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.980
Which means...

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.450
Yeah, it's already that time of year.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:12.410
I'm glad we remembered early this year.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.860
Tsubasa, nice assist.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:15.830
Um...

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:20.040
November 19th. 
It's Yashamaru-san's birthday.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:20.970
Oh...

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.850
What? Really?

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:27.000
He sulked last year 
since we forgot to text him.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:29.260
What should we do this year?

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:31.370
Should we send him a moth orchid?

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:35.180
How about a party? 
He likes flamboyant things.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:36.360
Good idea.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.530
We're going to be performing at the Dome,

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:40.100
so we should thank him 
for all his help day-to-day.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.600
Then let's make it a surprise party. 
A huge one.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:45.730
Where should we hold it?

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.640
If we're going to make a reservation, 
we should do it soon.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:50.660
How about holding it at home?

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:51.570
You're right.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.120
Home-cooked food would be 
a good way to show our appreciation.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:56.950
We can hold it in THRIVE's apartment.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.420
Hey, you can't just decide that.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:05.130
Yashamaru-san never comes 
because you never let anyone in.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.560
It might be a perfect way to keep it a secret.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.280
Then let's assign roles for 
food, presents, and decorations.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.430
Tsubasa, you'll help us, right?

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.310
Yes, of course.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.890
Good morning.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:28.150
<i>Yashamaru-san... is out all day today.</i>

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.150
Sooner would be better.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:37.300
<i>Good morning. This is Sumisora.</i>

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.660
What is it?

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:44.110
<i>B-Pro has something they want 
to discuss with you about the concert.</i>

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:50.540
Would you be able to come
to THRIVE's apartment at 9:00 PM

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:51.490
<i>on the 19th?</i>

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.550
Okay, I'm free then.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.240
Thank you.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:06.820
You can really see the difference 
between Kitakore and THRIVE with these.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:10.020
I wish it the shoulders allowed 
a little more movement, though.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:12.640
I made an appointment with Yashamaru-san.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:13.870
Thank you.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:16.490
Then let's go check it out tonight.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.250
Yeah, let's.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.970
Are you going somewhere?

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.870
Yeah, with the food team.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:24.820
Sumisora-san, would you like to come with us?

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:28.080
Italian, huh?

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.870
We thought it might inspire our own menu.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.480
The lasagna there is so good.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:35.550
You've all been there before?

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:40.760
A long time ago. 
Yashamaru-san treated us.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.630
Yashamaru-san did?

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:45.230
That's kind of surprising.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:50.540
Tsubasa-chan, you thought 
Yashamaru-san was cheap?

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.190
Th-That's not what I meant!

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:57.950
I've just never seen Yashamaru-san 
take you out to eat.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:02.200
Now that you mention it, 
we haven't since you came.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.700
Yashamaru-san has gotten even busier.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:09.960
He used to take us to all kinds 
of places until just recently.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.960
From expensive places to cheap places 
that prioritize quantity over quality.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:15.760
All kinds of restaurants.

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:18.540
We have a lot of growing boys in the group,

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:21.470
so it must've been hard 
on Yashamaru-san's wallet.

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:27.730
Come to think of it, there was one time when 
Yashamaru-san drank too much and passed out.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.600
Yeah, he did.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:30.480
What?

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:35.250
We took turns carrying Yashamaru-san 
all the way back to the apartment.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:37.070
He was so heavy.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:42.870
I learned what it meant 
to be truly at wit's end then.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.620
Yashamaru-san did that?

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.540
I've never seen anything like that before.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:54.330
Great smile! You're glowing!

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:00.590
Hey, everyone. How are Yashamaru-san's 
presents coming along?

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:04.720
I'm nearly done.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:08.980
Ryuji-kun, did you embroider that? 
That's amazing.

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.850
Well, it is my specialty.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.670
Ryuji even makes his own clothes.

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.360
Nome-san, your smart phone 
cover is amazing, too.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.780
I'm sure Yashamaru-san will love it.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:26.030
How are you so good with your hands 
when you look like a feral child?

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:28.940
All I had to do was put stickers on it.

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:30.190
There's no need to be sarcastic...

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.500
I messed up again.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:37.130
Is this a guitar pick?

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.440
Yeah.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.730
What? Does Yashamaru-san play the guitar?

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:44.140
He was in a band when he was younger.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:45.740
You didn't know?

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.420
No.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:49.960
He never went pro, though.

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.150
I'm learning so many new things about him.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:12:01.150
Now that I think about it, I hardly 
know anything about Yashamaru-san.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.240
You can't help that.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.240
We've known him for a really long time.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:11.210
Besides, Yashamaru-san's 
the one who chose us for B-Pro.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:15.920
He's been with us since 
before we could get any work.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:19.700
And until you showed up, 
he'd go with us to our jobs.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:25.990
He'd scold us, encourage us, and bow 
his head to important people for us.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:31.220
He brought B-Project this far.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:34.600
I see.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:38.260
He's like a mother to us.

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.720
Don't you mean a father?

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:41.200
More like a god.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.120
<i>I see.</i>

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:50.070
<i>The bond between the boys and Yashamaru-san 
is built on years of shared experiences.</i>

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:56.460
<i>Are you having trouble with anything?</i>

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.820
I'm fine for now.

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:01.300
<i>In that case, could you confirm the rehearsal?</i>

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.830
Sure. U-Um...

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:04.470
<i>What?</i>

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:08.270
Would you like to have 
dinner together sometime?

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:11.670
<i>Where did that come from?</i>

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:17.440
Well, we've been holding all 
our meetings over the phone lately.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.230
I thought we should get fired up 
in preparation for the Dome—

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:23.880
<i>Come to think of it, 
you've been acting weird lately.</i>

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:26.320
<i>You've been kind of fidgety.</i>

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:29.710
<i>You're not hiding something from me, are you?</i>

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:32.610
N-No! Nothing at all.

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:35.130
Sorry for bothering you when you're so busy.

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:37.170
Sorry. Good bye.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:46.090
I almost ruined the surprise 
by saying something I shouldn't have.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.260
I'm such an idiot.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.050
That should do it.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:03.930
You spelled it wrong.

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:04.650
No way!

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:08.610
The "th" in "birthday" is backwards.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:10.290
Huh? What's that?

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.220
I said...

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:14.650
You do it, Kane-chin!

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.490
We have to get this done 
before Yashamaru-san comes!

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.320
Who's going to get the wine?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.000
Sumisora-san said she'd get it.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.010
Miracle-rin-rin! Ru-ru-rin-rin!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.020
May this become a delicious acqua pazza!

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:31.390
It's perfect.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:33.260
All we have to do it wrap them.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:34.890
Kento, how's your pick?

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:39.020
Don't talk to me! My fingers slipped again.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.970
You're still working on that?

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.230
You're unbelievably clumsy 
for someone who arranges their bangs

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.730
down to the millimeter.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.420
Shut up.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.590
I'll help you. Let me see that.

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:51.700
You're hopeless. 
How many more do you have left?

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:55.200
Three, including this one.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:58.140
What? You've only finished one?

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:00.220
What have you been doing until today?

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:01.760
I've been working this whole time.

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:03.730
Hey, you monkey!

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:12.210
What kind of disgraceful combination 
of the Bon Festival and New Year's is this?

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:14.280
But it's festive.

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:17.720
Get rid of all this stuff!

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:20.730
Miracle-rin-rin! Ru-ru-rin-rin!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.480
May this become a delicious carpaccio!

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:29.970
It's so sweet.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.160
Yuta.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.860
I'm just tasting it.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:37.240
Massu, open up. Say "ah."

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.440
Just kidding.

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:42.330
Yuta.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:45.540
Mika, I smell something burning.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:46.260
Huh?

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:53.340
My herb-breaded sardines!

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:02.890
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:12.250
Thanks. That must've been tough in the rain.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:14.310
What do you think? Perfect, right?

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:16.610
You wouldn't expect less from us, right?

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:18.290
You guys shut up.

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:21.090
But it really is wonderful.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:24.040
I'm sure Yashamaru-san will love this.

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:26.960
Huh?

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:27.870
What?

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.690
I think I smell something burning...

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:33.510
It bothers you, too?

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:38.060
I'm sorry. I burned the food.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.020
We're running the fan.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.470
Wouldn't it be faster to open a window?

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:44.660
Wait, Hikaru!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.280
My bangs!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.760
You can't be serious!

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.780
What floor do you think we're on?

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:12.900
I'm sorry.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:16.120
Don't you know what'll happen 
if you open the window in this weather?

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:21.060
Now, now, Goshi. There are things we have 
to do before getting angry right now.

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:22.980
We have one more hour.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.600
Let's do whatever we can until then.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:28.640
The decorating group 
can clean up the apartment.

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:29.830
Yeah.

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.300
I'll help, too.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:36.860
We'll start by checking 
which ingredients we can still use

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:39.030
and come up with a menu from there.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:43.670
This isn't something we can 
save by cleaning, is it?

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:44.910
Yeah.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:47.740
Now we have nothing to give him.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:50.420
No, there is something.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:51.750
What?

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:53.770
Your music.

00:17:56.940 --> 00:18:03.060
This past week, I've felt the bond 
you share with Yashamaru-san.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.600
The gratitude and love you have for him.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:13.670
The best way to express that 
is through a B-Project performance.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:16.900
A concert, huh?

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:17.950
Great idea.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:19.010
Let's do it.

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:23.080
Tsubasa, could you throw 
together a B-Pro medley?

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:25.410
What? Me?

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:30.460
Can we edit it together 
in thirty and rehearse in thirty?

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:31.870
Tsubasa,

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:34.840
you just need to make something that conveys 
what you want to say to Yashamaru-san.

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:40.430
I understand. I'll give it my best shot.

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:43.100
Kaneshiro, I'll clean up instead.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:45.220
Can you help Sumisora?

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:46.220
Yeah.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:48.060
I'll come up with costumes.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.980
Kento, could you help clean up, too?

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:51.940
Okay.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:54.690
The first song is "Kodo Ambitious."

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.490
The moment you see the intro's shooting stars,

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:00.450
transition into the cotton 
candy clouds before the chorus.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:02.580
What? Which part?

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:06.340
What? At the edge of the vast universe,

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:09.250
the Earth slowly comes into view, 
then the moon beyond that.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:12.970
And right in the middle of it, 
there's a bright flash for a second.

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:14.210
I don't see that.

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:17.650
Let's get this done in twenty minutes.

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:18.670
Yeah.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.030
Build a stage?

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:24.640
Yeah, instead of decorations.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.720
Oh, right. It is a concert.

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:29.270
Let's do it by that wall.

00:19:33.890 --> 00:19:35.960
We don't have a platform 
to use as a raised stage.

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:38.480
But we can change the mood using lights.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:42.970
If we all wear similar tones 
and the same accessory...

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:49.970
That part should sound like 
approaching footsteps that suddenly stop.

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:50.910
Okay.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:57.720
Maybe this is where our concerts come from.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:19:59.170
What?

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:02.280
It doesn't matter how big the space is.

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.530
We just want to deliver our music 
to the people important to us.

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:08.180
We want them to be happy.

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:12.130
And we'll do everything 
we can do make that happen.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:16.440
We should approach the Dome 
concert with the same attitude.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:19.470
It's done.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:22.200
Here are the composition and the lyrics.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.730
Thanks.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:26.740
Way to go, A&R.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:27.950
You're welcome.

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:34.460
<i>It hasn't been long since I met them.</i>

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.960
<i>But now I'm one of the
people who supports B-Pro.</i>

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:47.240
<i>And I'm going to keep building my 
relationship with them and with Yashamaru-san.</i>

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:02.960
It's time.

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:04.810
Tsubasa-chan, how was that?

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:06.260
It was perfect.

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:08.910
Since you made it through RAIZIN, 
I know you can do it.

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:17.890
Goshi, put on your ribbon properly.

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:20.100
What? Isn't this good enough?

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:22.840
I hope Yashamaru-san comes soon.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:26.010
He can be pretty relaxed 
when it comes to his private life.

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:30.850
Maybe he had to work late.

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:33.240
I'll try calling him again.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:36.570
Should we go over our formation?

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:37.520
Yeah.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:38.380
Okay.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:45.990
He's late.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:48.490
Maybe he forgot.

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:51.870
<i>...can't come to the phone right now.</i>

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:56.250
He's not answering.

00:21:56.550 --> 00:21:58.800
Maybe he dropped his phone somewhere.

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:01.750
But he's apparently reading 
his "Join" messages.

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:05.510
<b>Yashamaru Sakutaro</b>

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:04.950
Maybe something came up.

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:10.530
It's after midnight.

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:17.160
Happy birthday, Yashamaru-san.

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:24.220
<i>Yashamaru-san...</i>

00:23:55.850 --> 00:23:57.850
Quit looking at me and go to sleep.

00:23:57.850 --> 00:23:59.340
I'll be right beside you.
